From ac22f82f349f7aa91d975b82d6a51b7fa1641315 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:31:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] provider: a plugin saying a built-in icon's name for its
 provider had it shown

A plugin provider's icon was the picture its auth hook or package.json
gave (kept as a user's picture is) or the market's, and a bare name said
in either place was refused by both readers: host.js's iconOf carried
only an https URL or a data:image URI, and pluginOwnIcon asked iconURL
of it, which takes a URL. The market's own bare names went through
(MarketIcon), so a plugin the market lists showed its mark and one
installed by hand showed the generic glyph, whatever it said (#5103).

A bare name (no scheme, no path) now passes both readers as it is, as a
market name does; the page draws it from its bundled icons, falling back
to the generic glyph for one it has no file of. A picture is still
checked, fetched and kept as before.

Fixes #5103

Generated-by: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode)
